---
import { opportunities } from '../../lib/clients/wheeler-backlinks';
const sortedOpportunities = [...opportunities].sort((a,b) => Number(b.status === 'Done') - Number(a.status === 'Done'));
const scorecard = [
 ['Referring domains, raw count','4','1,877','54'],
 ['Genuine referring domains','3','4','3'],
 ['Automated spam domains','1','About 1,870','About 50'],
 ['Toxic links needing action','None','Not Wheeler’s site','Only relevant if redirected'],
 ['Disavow file needed','No','Not applicable','Not applicable'],
 ['Anchor text','Branded URL, “Visit Website” and image links','Dominated by link-selling spam text','Partly link-selling spam text']
];
const types = [
 ['Link-selling spam','515','Automated pages that insert domains into link-building advertisements.','onvaxs.com; 888ph.online'],
 ['URL-shortener and website-report pages','21','Auto-generated domain reports and shortener pages.','bye.fyi/report; anchorurl.cloud/share; urls-shortener.eu; screenshots.wiki'],
 ['Auto-generated rank pages','5','Throwaway pages on free hosting.','global-ranks.pages.dev; huldra.pages.dev'],
 ['Same-owner redirect','1','The other business’s alternate domain.','wheelersupply.com'],
 ['Genuine','4','One editorial article and three business directories.','buildsteel.org; yellowpages.com; superpages.com; dexknows.com']
];
---
<div class="backlink-audit">
  <header class="workspace-heading backlink-heading"><div><h1>Wheeler backlink strategy</h1></div><div class="review-overview"><strong>getwheelersteel.com</strong><small>Updated 19 October 2026</small></div></header>
  <section class="audit-latest-update" data-backlink-update-version="2026-10-19" aria-labelledby="audit-latest-update-heading">
    <div class="audit-update-heading"><span class="audit-update-eyebrow">Latest audit update</span><time datetime="2026-10-19">Checked 19 October 2026</time></div>
    <h2 id="audit-latest-update-heading">What changed since October 6</h2>
    <div class="audit-update-summary"><div><strong>2 → 4</strong><span>Wheeler referring domains</span></div><p>A new Malibu Chamber link and more Palibu listings. The audit also includes refreshed competitor data and Google search findings.</p></div>
    <p class="audit-update-next"><strong>Next priorities:</strong> a link from Don’s older website, relevant directories and new partner coverage.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="workspace-tabs backlink-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Backlink views"><button id="view-backlink-audit" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel-backlink-audit" tabindex="0">Audit and data</button><button id="view-backlink-actions" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-backlink-actions" tabindex="-1">Actions</button></div>
  <section id="panel-backlink-audit" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="view-backlink-audit">
  <p class="backlink-tab-intro">Build authority through new industry coverage of Wheeler’s current work and consistent listings.</p>
  <div class="audit-highlights"><div><span>WHEELER</span><strong>4 <span class="audit-count-change" aria-label="Up 2 referring domains since October 6">↑ 2</span><small>indexed referring domains</small></strong><small class="audit-history">Was 2 on October 6</small><p>3 genuine · 1 automated spam</p></div><div><span>WHEELERSTEELSUPPLY.COM</span><strong>1,877 <span class="audit-count-change" aria-label="Up 1,331 referring domains since October 6">↑ 1,331</span><small>indexed referring domains</small></strong><small class="audit-history">Was 546 on October 6</small><p>4 genuine · about 1,870 automated spam</p></div><div><span>DON’S OLDER WEBSITE</span><strong>54 <span class="audit-count-change" aria-label="Up 9 referring domains since October 6">↑ 9</span><small>indexed referring domains</small></strong><small class="audit-history">Was 45 on October 6</small><p>3 genuine · about 50 automated spam</p><a class="audit-domain-link" href="http://donwheelerconstruction.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">donwheelerconstruction.com ↗</a></div></div>
  <div class="audit-overview-grid">
    <div class="audit-profile-stack">
    <section class="audit-panel audit-profile" aria-labelledby="link-profile-heading"><div class="audit-panel-heading"><h2 id="link-profile-heading">The link profile</h2><span class="audit-status done">No toxic links for Wheeler</span></div><p class="audit-note">Compare genuine links, not just raw totals.</p><div class="audit-table-wrap"><table class="audit-scorecard"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Metric</th><th scope="col">Wheeler</th><th scope="col">wheelersteelsupply.com</th><th scope="col">Don’s older site</th></tr></thead><tbody>{scorecard.map(row=><tr>{row.map((cell,index)=>index===0?<th scope="row">{cell}</th>:<td data-label={['Metric','Wheeler','wheelersteelsupply.com','Don’s older site'][index]}>{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="audit-note">Wheeler’s one spam domain (<a href="https://seonix.agency/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">seonix.agency</a>, nofollow) appeared on October 11. Every website collects a few of these. No action is needed.</p></section>
    <section class="audit-panel"><div class="audit-panel-heading"><h2>Already in place</h2><span class="audit-status done">5 assets</span></div><div class="audit-existing"><article><span class="audit-status done">Done</span> <span class="audit-status audit-new">New</span><h3><a href="https://malibuchamberofcommerce.growthzoneapp.com/business-directory/FindStartsWith?term=W" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Malibu Chamber of Commerce directory ↗</a></h3><p>The Chamber’s directory platform now links to Wheeler. Dofollow, spam score 0. First seen October 17, 2026.</p></article><article><span class="audit-status done">Done</span><h3><a href="https://business.palibu.org/rebuild-partners" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Palisades Rebuild Partners ↗</a></h3><p>A locally relevant business-directory link. Spam score 0, dofollow and a branded URL anchor. Palibu also added three category pages linking to Wheeler on October 9.</p></article><article><span class="audit-status done">Done</span><h3><a href="https://www.buildersshow.com/Search/Exhibitor.aspx?id=1533073&year=2027" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IBS 2027 exhibitor listing ↗</a></h3><p>A clean trade-industry link. Dofollow, with an image-link anchor.</p></article><article><span class="audit-status done">Done</span><h3><a href="https://cfsei.memberclicks.net/index.php?option=com_community&view=profile&userid=2019503038" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CFSEI member profile ↗</a></h3><p><a href="https://www.cfsei.org/index.php?option=com_community&amp;pageNum=140&amp;view=search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public CFSEI directory ↗</a></p><p>Public CFSEI listings name Wheeler Residential Steel Supply and its website. They count as mentions, not backlinks, because the website address is not a clickable link.</p></article><article><span class="audit-status done">Done</span><h3>Google Business Profile</h3><p>Already in place and managed by Wheeler’s team.</p></article></div><p class="audit-note">Wheeler’s indexed links were first seen between October 2 and 17, 2026.</p></section>
    </div>
    <div class="audit-profile-stack"><section class="audit-panel audit-explainer"><div class="audit-panel-heading"><h2>Competitor link audit</h2></div><p><strong>1,877 domains. Still four genuine sources.</strong></p><p>The indexed total rose from 546 to 1,877 between October 6 and 19. The increase is automated spam from one bulk network of throwaway sites (.store, .shop, .site, .space, .website and .online). The genuine links are unchanged: one editorial article and three directory listings.</p><div class="audit-competitor-context" aria-labelledby="ranking-context-heading"><h2 id="ranking-context-heading">Why the established Wheeler website can rank ahead today</h2><p><strong>It has a head start.</strong> The older website has had more time to establish its pages, business mentions and relevant links. It is reasonable to expect that established presence to lead a new website in some Google results, especially searches for the Wheeler name.</p><p><strong>This is not 1,877 useful endorsements.</strong> This audit identifies four genuine referring domains versus Wheeler’s three. The priority is to connect credible coverage to the correct company and build relevant authority. This audit does not establish rankings across every search.</p></div><h3 class="audit-breakdown-heading">Breakdown as of October 6 (546 domains)</h3><div class="audit-table-wrap"><table class="audit-types"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Link type</th><th scope="col">Count</th></tr></thead><tbody>{types.map(row=><tr><th scope="row"><strong>{row[0]}</strong><p>{row[2]}</p><small>{row[3].split('; ').map((domain,index)=><>{index>0&&'; '}<a href={`https://${domain}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{domain} ↗</a></>)}</small></th><td data-label="Count">{row[1]}</td></tr>)}<tr><th scope="row"><strong>Added October 6 to 19</strong><p>Automated spam from one bulk network.</p></th><td data-label="Count">1,331</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="audit-note">Automated spam links are aimed at almost every small business site without the owner’s involvement. These counts do not imply the other company purchased links.</p><p class="audit-note">Search engines generally discount automated spam links, so the surge does not strengthen the other website.</p></section>
    <section class="audit-panel" aria-labelledby="website-changes-heading"><div class="audit-panel-heading"><h2 id="website-changes-heading">Changes on the other Wheeler website</h2><span class="audit-status audit-new">New</span></div><ul class="audit-update-list"><li>The other Wheeler website republished all six of its pages on October 6, 2026.</li><li>It no longer references Don Wheeler’s work or project photos. Several older photos and its project portfolio section were removed. Its Projects page is no longer in the main menu.</li><li>This makes the separation between the two businesses clearer for search engines and AI assistants.</li></ul><p class="audit-note">Compared against archived copies of the site from March to July 2026. We check for further changes with each audit refresh.</p></section>
    <section class="audit-panel" aria-labelledby="search-results-heading"><div class="audit-panel-heading"><h2 id="search-results-heading">Search results, October 19</h2><span class="audit-status audit-new">New</span></div><p class="audit-note">Los Angeles, desktop Google. Results vary by location and day.</p><div class="audit-table-wrap"><table class="audit-search-results"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Search</th><th scope="col">What appears</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">“Wheeler Steel Framing Supply”</th><td data-label="What appears"><span class="audit-status audit-new">New</span> Wheeler’s <a href="https://business.palibu.org/business-directory/details/wheeler-residential-steel-supply-5030829" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Palibu listing ↗</a> ranks #2. Palibu pages for Wheeler appear three more times in the top 20.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">“Don Wheeler Steel”</th><td data-label="What appears">Map results show both businesses side by side.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">“Wheeler Residential Steel Supply”</th><td data-label="What appears">Wheeler’s Business Profile panel shows. The website itself is not yet in the top 20 results.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Indexed pages</th><td data-label="What appears">8 of 10. The two newest pages are not indexed yet.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="audit-note">The main gap is still ranking for Wheeler’s own name. The actions on the next tab address it.</p></section>
    </div>
  </div>
  </section>
  <section id="panel-backlink-actions" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="view-backlink-actions" hidden>
    <section class="audit-panel audit-priorities"><p class="eyebrow">PRIORITY ACTIONS</p><h2>Start here this month</h2><ol class="audit-quick-wins"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Link from Don’s older website</strong><p>Add a plain link to <a href="https://getwheelersteel.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">getwheelersteel.com ↗</a> from <a href="http://donwheelerconstruction.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Don’s older website ↗</a>. Make this the first link priority.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Consistent directory listings</strong><p><a href="https://www.yellowpages.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YellowPages ↗</a>, <a href="https://www.superpages.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Superpages ↗</a> and <a href="https://www.dexknows.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DexKnows ↗</a> with matching name, address and phone.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Partner link from ESRL Development</strong><p>A link from <a href="https://esrldevelopment.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wheeler’s installation partner’s website ↗</a> would be directly relevant.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><strong>New BuildSteel / SFIA story pitch</strong><p>The Palisades rebuild, IBS 2027 or the Palisades Recovery Expo.</p></div></li></ol><a class="audit-action-link" href="#backlink-opportunities">See all {opportunities.length} opportunities ↓</a></section>
  <section class="audit-panel audit-action-panel" id="backlink-opportunities" aria-labelledby="backlink-opportunities-heading"><div class="audit-panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE ACTION PLAN</p><h2 id="backlink-opportunities-heading">Backlink opportunities</h2><p class="audit-note">Completed actions appear first. Open means proposed, not completed.</p></div><div class="audit-filter"><label for="backlink-status-filter">Show status</label><select id="backlink-status-filter"><option value="all">All opportunities</option><option value="Done">Done</option><option value="Open">Open</option><option value="No action">No action</option><option value="To check">To check</option></select></div></div><p id="backlink-filter-count" class="audit-result-count" role="status">{opportunities.length} opportunities</p><div class="audit-table-wrap"><table class="audit-opportunity-table"><colgroup><col class="opportunity-checkbox-col" /><col class="opportunity-name-col" /><col class="opportunity-action-col" /><col class="opportunity-status-col" /></colgroup><thead><tr><th scope="col">Done</th><th scope="col">Opportunity &amp; current finding</th><th scope="col">Next action</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{sortedOpportunities.map((item,index)=><tr data-backlink-id={item.id} data-backlink-order={opportunities.findIndex(opportunity => opportunity.id === item.id)} data-initial-status={item.status} data-backlink-status={item.status} id={`backlink-opportunity-${item.id}`}><td class="audit-completion">{item.status!=='No action'&&<label><input type="checkbox" data-backlink-checkbox={item.id} checked={item.status==='Done'} aria-label={`Mark ${item.title} as done`} /></label>}</td><th scope="row"><div class="audit-opportunity-name"><span class="audit-number">{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div>{item.logo && <img class="audit-platform-logo" src={item.logo} width="20" height="20" alt="" />}{item.url?<a href={item.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{item.title} ↗</a>:<strong>{item.title}</strong>}<p>{item.finding}</p>{item.links&&<div class="audit-directory-links">{item.links.map(link=><a href={link.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{link.name} ↗</a>)}</div>}</div></div></th><td data-label="Next action" class="audit-next-action"><strong>{item.action}</strong></td><td data-label="Status"><span data-backlink-badge class:list={['audit-status',item.status==='Done'?'done':item.status==='No action'?'no-action':item.status==='Open'?'open':'check']}>{item.status}</span></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p id="backlink-save-status" class="audit-note" role="status" hidden></p><button id="retry-backlink-save" type="button" hidden>Retry saving</button><p class="audit-note">Audit findings were updated October 19. Completion statuses include subsequent updates. Check an opportunity when completed. Completion is saved to the shared workspace.</p></section>

  </section>
</div>

<style>
 .audit-highlights .audit-count-change{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:middle;margin-left:8px;padding:4px 7px;border-radius:5px;background:#edf4ef;color:#285c45;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0;line-height:1.2;}.audit-highlights strong>small{display:block;margin-top:8px;}

 .audit-latest-update{margin:0 0 28px;padding:22px 24px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #cbd9d0;border-left:3px solid #285c45;border-radius:10px;}
 .audit-update-heading{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:12px;color:#52665a;}
 .audit-update-eyebrow{color:#285c45;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;}
 .audit-latest-update h2{font-size:19px;line-height:1.35;margin:12px 0 16px;}
 .audit-update-summary{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:24px;}.audit-update-summary>div{flex-shrink:0;padding-right:24px;border-right:1px solid #dce5df;}
 .audit-update-summary strong{display:block;font-size:26px;line-height:1.2;color:#214f3d;}.audit-update-summary span{display:block;font-size:12px;margin-top:5px;color:#52665a;}
 .audit-update-summary p,.audit-update-next{font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;margin:0;}.audit-update-next{margin-top:18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e3eae5;color:#465b4e;}
 @media(max-width:600px){.audit-latest-update{padding:18px;}.audit-update-summary{align-items:flex-start;gap:16px;flex-direction:column;}.audit-update-summary>div{border-right:0;padding-right:0;}}

 .audit-new{color:#285777;background:#eaf2f8;border-color:#c7d8e6;}
 .audit-history{display:block;color:#68756d;font-size:11px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:8px;}
 .audit-breakdown-heading{font-size:14px;margin-top:24px;}
 .audit-update-list{padding-left:20px;margin-top:16px;}.audit-update-list li+li{margin-top:12px;}
 .audit-search-results th{width:38%;}.audit-search-results td{line-height:1.65;}
 @media(max-width:600px){.audit-highlights .audit-history{grid-column:1;grid-row:auto;}.audit-search-results th{width:100%;}}
</style>
